From: axon7m bring-up
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: s6e3ha3: the backlight scale is linear

The panel's DCS brightness (0x51) sets the AMOLED luminance directly; the
perceptual curve is the user interface's job. With the scale "unknown",
drm_hwcomposer applies the HLG OETF on top of Android's own curve: 10 %
brightness gave 138 of 255 (LineageOS 24 run 29) and the slider's low end
stayed bright. Report BACKLIGHT_SCALE_LINEAR so drm_hwc writes the value
as it is.
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-samsung-s6e3ha3.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-samsung-s6e3ha3.c
index 2353ac130..bac0cdc75 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-samsung-s6e3ha3.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-samsung-s6e3ha3.c
@@ -206,6 +206,7 @@ static int s6e3ha3_probe(struct mipi_dsi_device *dsi)
 	};
 	const struct backlight_properties bl_props = {
 		.type = BACKLIGHT_RAW,
+		.scale = BACKLIGHT_SCALE_LINEAR,
 		.brightness = 160,
 		.max_brightness = 255,
 	};
